{title: 234 - Christ Is the World's Light}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #234 • CHRISTE SANCTORUM • 5.10.6.11.6}
{lyricist: Fred Pratt Green}
{composer: Paris Antiphoner}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 234}
{meta: tune CHRISTE SANCTORUM}
{meta: meter 5.10.6.11.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F#m]Christ is [Em/B]the [D/A]world's [A]Light,
[Bm]He and [F#m/C#]none [D]other; born [F#m/C#]in [Bm]our [A]darkness,
[Bm]He became [A]our [Em]brother.
[D/A]If [A7/G]we [A]have [A7]seen [D]Him, [G]we have [D/F#]seen the [A]Father:
[D/A]Glory to [A]God on [D/F#]high!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F#m]Christ is [Em/B]the [D/A]world's [A]Peace,
[Bm]He and [F#m/C#]none [D]other; no [F#m/C#]one [Bm]can [A]serve [D/A]Him
[Bm]and despise [A]another.
[D/A]Who [A7/G]else [Bm/F#]unites [G]us one in [Em/B]God [D/A]the [F#m]Father?
[D/A]Glory to [A]God on [D/F#]high!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F#m]Christ is [Em/B]the [D/A]world'sLife,
[Bm]He and [F#m/C#]none [D]other; sold [F#m/C#]once [Bm]for [A]silver,
[D/A]murdered here, [G]our [Em/B]broher,
[D/A]He who redeems us [A]reigns with God the [D/F#]Father.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F#m]Give God [Em/B]the [D/A]glory,
[Bm]God and [F#m/C#]none [D]other; give [F#m/C#]God [Bm]the [A]glory,
[D/A]Spirit, [A]Son, [A7]and [D]Father; [G/D]give [D/F#]God the [A]glory,
[D/A]God in Man my brother; [A]Glory to God [D/F#]on high!
{end_of_verse}
